--- reading it --------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. S00ota-clock works as a script and does not hold: the line at 23:10:35 is followed by the
   RTC driver's own "setting system clock to 2000-01-01" at 23:10:38, and `date` at the prompt
   says 2000. The log line of ota-health shows 2000-01-01 too, written after the raise.
   Cause: CONFIG_RTC_DRV_OMAP=m, loaded by mdev; fix: =y. The clock at power-on is 1970, and
   2000-01-01 is the RTC's own value, which corrects "cold-boots into 2000" in earlier notes.
2. S99ota-health refused to confirm a healthy slot. RAUC_SYSTEM_BOOTED_BOOTNAME holds the
   device path here, not "A". The failure is the safe one: BOOT_A_LEFT stayed at 2, so with no
   fix three such boots would have retired the only good slot and landed in the last-resort path.
3. Everything else held: slot A selected with its attempt counted, root read-only, /data
   read-write and mounted, rauc status and fw_printenv agree on the state, the failure reason
   reached /data/ota-health.log (FR-014), and boot status "bad" for the never-written slot B.
